% # US Salary Data 2026: 350k Job Postings: findings, method and data card
%
% > US salary data 2026: 350,000 job postings with posted pay in US$ per year by role, seniority, state, metro area and industry, Jan 2024 to Jun 2026.
%
% *Fliar Research | released October 2026 | licence CC BY-NC 4.0*
%
% **How this dataset was acquired.** Every row comes from the [Radar API](https://github.com/fliarbi/radar-api-mcp), Fliar's company-data API and MCP server. Radar reads
% public job postings from job boards and company career pages every day and parses each one into structured fields: title, employer,
% location, work mode, experience asked, category and pay. This release keeps the United States postings that state pay, published between
% January 2024 and June 2026, removes re-posts of the same job, and annualises every pay figure (hourly, weekly, monthly or annual) to
% **US dollars per year**. It is built for salary benchmarking by role family, seniority, state, metro area, industry and experience. It holds
% no job descriptions, application links or recruiter names. Salary statistics for any title, city and skill set, refreshed daily, are served
% by `POST /v1/jobs/salary-benchmark` ([reference](https://github.com/fliarbi/radar-api-mcp/blob/main/docs/reference/salary_benchmark.md)) or the `salary_benchmark` MCP tool; the postings themselves by `POST /v1/jobs/search`.
%
% > **This file is a 25% sample: 88,798 of 350,328 job postings with pay.** It keeps every record for a fixed subset of companies.
% > The subset is chosen by a hash, so it stays the same from one release to the next. The findings and tables below were computed
% > on the **full** data. For the rest, the withheld fields and monthly updates, [get a Radar API key](https://fliarbi.com/radar-api/developer) ([docs](https://github.com/fliarbi/radar-api-mcp)).
% > Each row's `fliar_profile_url` opens the company's full profile on Fliar.
%
% ## Key findings
%
% 1. **350,328 US job postings that state pay, from 73,471 employers**, posted January 2024 to June 2026 (222,579 in 2026). The median posted pay is **$60,000 a year** (middle half $41,600 to $97,500).
% 2. **53% of postings quote an hourly rate** and 44% an annual salary; hourly postings annualise (x 2,080 hours) to a median $43,680, against $88,000 for annual-salary postings.
% 3. **DevOps & cloud has the highest median** ($126,950), then software engineering ($120,805) and product & project management ($115,000); retail & hospitality is lowest ($36,816).
% 4. **Highest-paying states** (1,000+ postings): District of Columbia ($85,000), California ($70,000) and New York ($68,640); lowest: Oklahoma ($45,760). California holds 22% of postings.
% 5. **San Francisco-Oakland-Berkeley is the best-paying large metro** (median $98,500), ahead of San Jose-Sunnyvale-Santa Clara ($96,550); Jacksonville is lowest among metros with 1,000+ postings ($49,000).
% 6. **Seniority ladder**: entry $41,600, mid $70,000, senior $100,000, manager $83,200, director $130,000; remote-marked postings pay a median $88,000 against $59,700 onsite.
%
% ## This OpenML copy
%
% An ML-ready cut of the public sample file: 88,798 of its 88,798 rows, keeping only rows where the default target `salary_mid_usd` is present.
% The free-text and URL columns (fliar_profile_url) are removed here. Columns that give the target away (salary_min_usd, salary_max_usd) are removed too. The original sample, with each row's Fliar company profile link,
% the full report (findings, tables, method, limitations) and the PDF are on Kaggle and Hugging Face:
%
% - Kaggle: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/harshitkz/us-salary-benchmarks-2026
% - Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/datasets/HarshitKZ/us-salary-benchmarks-2026
%
% Identifier and name columns are kept but marked as ignore attributes.
%
% ## Columns
%
% - `posting_id`: stable 12-character ID of the posting (a hash, not the source ID)
% - `posted_month`: month the posting was published (YYYY-MM)
% - `company`: hiring company name as posted
% - `company_domain`: company website domain when the name matches exactly one US company in Fliar's index, else blank
% - `job_title`: job title as posted (phone/e-mail-like strings removed)
% - `role_family`: role family (from the posting, else inferred from the title, else from the category)
% - `seniority`: intern / entry / mid / senior / lead / manager / director / executive; blank when neither title nor experience gives a signal
% - `experience_band`: minimum experience asked, banded; blank when not stated
% - `city`: city
% - `state`: two-letter state code
% - `metro`: metro area when the city is one of its principal cities, else blank
% - `industry_category`: industry / occupation group (occupation codes mapped to their major group, free text normalised)
% - `remote`: onsite / remote / hybrid when stated
% - `pay_period`: pay period as posted: hourly, weekly, monthly or annual
% - `salary_mid_usd`: midpoint of the range (or the single figure), US$ per year
%
% Licence: CC BY-NC 4.0. Attribution: Fliar BI (https://fliarbi.com). Contact: b2b@fliarbi.com.
%
@RELATION fliarbi-us-salary-postings-2026

@ATTRIBUTE posting_id STRING
@ATTRIBUTE posted_month {2024-01, 2024-02, 2024-03, 2024-04, 2024-05, 2024-06, 2024-07, 2024-08, 2024-09, 2024-10, 2024-11, 2024-12, 2025-01, 2025-02, 2025-03, 2025-04, 2025-05, 2025-06, 2025-07, 2025-08, 2025-09, 2025-10, 2025-11, 2025-12, 2026-01, 2026-02, 2026-03, 2026-04, 2026-05, 2026-06}
@ATTRIBUTE company STRING
@ATTRIBUTE company_domain STRING
@ATTRIBUTE job_title STRING
@ATTRIBUTE role_family {admin, construction, customer-service, data, design, devops-cloud, education, finance, healthcare, hr, it-support, legal, logistics, manufacturing, marketing, operations, other, product, retail-hospitality, sales, science-research, security, software-eng}
@ATTRIBUTE seniority {director, entry, executive, intern, lead, manager, mid, senior}
@ATTRIBUTE experience_band {'0-1 yrs', '11-15 yrs', '16+ yrs', '2-3 yrs', '4-6 yrs', '7-10 yrs'}
@ATTRIBUTE city STRING
@ATTRIBUTE state {AK, AL, AR, AZ, CA, CO, CT, DC, DE, FL, GA, HI, IA, ID, IL, IN, KS, KY, LA, MA, MD, ME, MI, MN, MO, MS, MT, NC, ND, NE, NH, NJ, NM, NV, NY, OH, OK, OR, PA, RI, SC, SD, TN, TX, UT, VA, VT, WA, WI, WV, WY}
@ATTRIBUTE metro {Albuquerque, 'Atlanta-Sandy Springs-Alpharetta', 'Austin-Round Rock-Georgetown', Baltimore-Columbia-Towson, Boise, Boston-Cambridge-Newton, Charlotte-Concord-Gastonia, Chicago-Naperville-Elgin, Cincinnati, Cleveland-Elyria, Columbus, 'Dallas-Fort Worth-Arlington', Denver-Aurora-Lakewood, Detroit-Warren-Dearborn, Hartford, Honolulu, 'Houston-The Woodlands-Sugar Land', Indianapolis-Carmel, Jacksonville, 'Kansas City', 'Las Vegas-Henderson-Paradise', 'Los Angeles-Long Beach-Anaheim', Louisville, Memphis, 'Miami-Fort Lauderdale-West Palm Beach', Milwaukee-Waukesha, 'Minneapolis-St. Paul-Bloomington', Nashville-Davidson-Franklin, 'New York-Newark-Jersey City', 'Oklahoma City', Omaha, Orlando-Kissimmee-Sanford, Philadelphia-Camden-Wilmington, Phoenix-Mesa-Chandler, Pittsburgh, Portland-Vancouver-Hillsboro, Raleigh-Cary, 'Riverside-San Bernardino-Ontario', 'Rochester (NY)', Sacramento-Roseville, 'Salt Lake City', 'San Antonio-New Braunfels', 'San Diego-Chula Vista-Carlsbad', 'San Francisco-Oakland-Berkeley', 'San Jose-Sunnyvale-Santa Clara', Seattle-Tacoma-Bellevue, Spokane, 'St. Louis', 'Tampa-St. Petersburg-Clearwater', 'Virginia Beach-Norfolk-Newport News', Washington-Arlington-Alexandria}
@ATTRIBUTE industry_category {'Admin & Office Support', Agriculture, 'Banking, Finance & Accounts', 'Community & Social Service', 'Construction & Real Estate', 'Customer Service & BPO', 'Education & Training', 'Engineering & Manufacturing', 'Facilities & Maintenance', 'Healthcare & Pharma', 'Hospitality & Food', 'Human Resources', 'Legal & Compliance', 'Logistics & Supply Chain', 'Marketing, Media & Communications', Military, 'Operations & Consulting', 'Personal Care & Services', 'Retail & E-commerce', 'Sales & Business Development', 'Science & Research', 'Security & Protective Services', 'Software & IT'}
@ATTRIBUTE remote {hybrid, onsite, remote}
@ATTRIBUTE pay_period {annual, bi-weekly, hourly, monthly, semi-monthly, weekly}
@ATTRIBUTE salary_mid_usd INTEGER

@DATA
